{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_27c03e1589f94b7980361c4575978ee7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There's a `main.cc` and the build uses `-lFuzzingEngine` (OSS-Fuzz). The `FUZZING_CPPFLAGS` comes from OSS-Fuzz which defines the custom allocator. Let me check if `main.cc` exists and look for the allocator definition.\n\nThe OSS-Fuzz build for harfbuzz 1.4.4 era included a custom allocator to simulate OOM. This is the crux of the \"OOM\" bug. The key insight: the fuzzer is compiled so that certain allocations FAIL, exposing invalid buffer access. Let me check main.cc.\n\n \n \n\n\n"}],"model":"DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731","usage":{"input_tokens":45616,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"797f274e-a18b-426c-8154-8e32629cfe04","uuid":"44e08ba0-0bb8-4df7-8f18-c73d41ecaaa8"}
