ame behavior.\n\nWait — maybe the seed font, when processed, does NOT reach a state where hb_buffer_create fails because memory is fine. But if the arvo repro sets rss_limit LOW (say 8MB), then even a 2KB font... the process uses ~2KB input + harfbuzz allocs (~few KB) + ASan (~small). That's <8MB, no OOM. So seed fine. For a crash, need the font to push past 8MB — a maxed font (4-6MB allocs) might not reach 8MB either.\n\nThe gap (8MB) is very low; a maxed 65535-lookup font allocating ~4MB of accels + engine could approach it. Let me try the maxed font! If the limit were e.g. 6-8MB, the maxed font might just tip it, and hb_buffer_create fails → crash.\n\nThis is plausible! Let me build a maxed-out font and submit. Even if it doesn't crash, it's evidence.\n\nLet me build a font with:\n- maxp numGlyphs = 65535\n- GSUB with lookupList len = 65535 (empty/valid lookups)\n- GPOS same\n- cmap mapping\n\nBuilding 65535 lookups in GSUB requires the font to be big-ish (~700KB). Let me build it.\n\nLet me write the builder. This is involved but let me do it.\n\nActually — reconsider HB_SANITIZE_MAX_EDITS=3 in fuzzing build. Sanitizing a GSUB with 65535 lookups might be fine if valid. But building 65535 valid lookups is a lot. Let me build a GSUB with lookupList containing 65535 offsets all pointing to a shared valid single-substitution-lookup region. Offsets relative to lookupList start; all same relative offset → all offsets identical (0x... to the shared lookup). That's allowed.\n\nLookupList: len(2 bytes) + 65535 offset entries (2 bytes each) = 2 + 131070 = 131072 bytes, then the shared regions (ScriptList, FeatureList must come first in GSUB layout: header, scriptList offset, featureList offset, lookupList offset; then ScriptList, FeatureList, LookupList). Offsets are from start of GSUB table.\n\nThis is doable but intricate. Let me write it carefully.\n\nGiven the effort, let me do it in Python.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether 65535 lookups even gets reached. `hb_o